{"name":"Celestial Crown","hex":"#ead97c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"celestial crown","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A modified eastern crown consisting of a gold fence usually adorned with points or rays topped with stars of the same metal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celestial_crown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Celestial crown","blocks":[{"text":"The celestial crown is a modified version of the Eastern crown. The celestial crown is a representative badge or headdress consisting of a gold fence usually adorned with pointed points or rays topped with stars of the same metal. It usually has eight points, five in the representations that are not in relief, although the number of these is variable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Celestial_Crown.svg/330px-Celestial_Crown.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celestial_crown","wikidata":"Q16553123"},{"title":"Crown","blocks":[{"text":"A crown is a traditional form of head adornment, or hat, worn by monarchs as a symbol of their power and dignity. A crown is often, by extension, a symbol of the monarch's government or items endorsed by it. The word itself is used, particularly in Commonwealth countries, as an abstract name for the monarchy itself as distinct from the individual who inhabits it. A specific type of crown is employed in heraldry under strict rules. Indeed, some monarchies never had a physical crown, just a heraldic representation, to wit the constitutional kingdom of Belgium."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Saint_Edward%27s_Crown.jpg/330px-Saint_Edward%27s_Crown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crown","wikidata":"Q170984"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Lucia_%2831528327081%29.jpg/120px-Lucia_%2831528327081%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Lucia_%2831528327081%29.jpg/250px-Lucia_%2831528327081%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Lucia_%2831528327081%29.jpg/120px-Lucia_%2831528327081%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALucia_(31528327081).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/King_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_BCE.jpg/250px-King_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/King_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/King_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_BCE.jpg/250px-King_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crown of King of Persis Ardakhshir II, 1st century BC.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKing_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_CE.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Iron_Crown.JPG/500px-Iron_Crown.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Iron_Crown.JPG/1280px-Iron_Crown.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Iron_Crown.JPG/500px-Iron_Crown.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The Iron Cr